commit message:
This is a simple update to kate Calvin's commit from yesterday where VS 8 didn't have a problem with a pow with a double exponent but VS 7 wanted an int.  Will not affect results but will allow model to compile on VS 7.  Changed the exponent from 4.0 to 4

return QUADCOEF * pow( mMatureAge - MAXMATUREAGE, 4);
}

Clear up NAMESPACE inconsistencies

Inconsistencies in `importFrom`s were borking things - thanks
@russellhz for finding

Documentation fix

@swaldhoff can you review this asap please? It’s solid—should not take
much time.

Upgrade minimum R required

@kdorheim found that `startWith` not used in older versions of R.
Requiring 3.1.2, same as dplyr v0.7, seems reasonable.

@bpbond comments done

passed check package prior to these spacing changes, so it should still
pass. My heart can't deal with waiting on it again

ODA-374
Looking to the results of the reaction_advection model we noticed a strange periodical drop in standard deviation of the ensemble.

The problem is caused by a rounding issue in 
private void propagateNoiseModelsAndAddNoiseToExchangeItems(ITime currentTime, ITime targetTime) 

In matching the model times to noise model times we have a test

if(time>this.lastNoiseTimes.get(modelExchangeItemId)){

When the noise model and model make the same time steps, this test is very likely to give an unwanted result due to timy rounding errors. Is should be changed into 

if(time>this.lastNoiseTimes.get(modelExchangeItemId)+0.5*timePrecision){

Taking roudning errors into account. The factor 0.5 is used as an additional safeguard since times are compared (using timePrecision) within the if block.

ODA-455, ODA-459;
Revert trih-cadagno_netcdf.nc to r593.


